  "about.description": "The application finds DJI remote controllers on the local network or connects to an IP address. It displays controller details and the state of sticks, dials, the flight-mode switch, and buttons. Virtual-gamepad axes and buttons are mapped separately, analog controls can be inverted, and the mapping is saved in the configuration.\n\nDiscovery, connection, and monitoring work on Linux, Windows, and macOS. Linux emulation uses /dev/uinput and requests system authorization when direct access is unavailable. A configured vJoy device is required on 64-bit Windows. macOS and other platforms do not support a virtual gamepad.\n\nDJI RC and DJI RC 2 have been verified. DJI RC Pro, DJI Smart Controller, and DJI RC Pro Enterprise are expected to be compatible, but remain untested. Discovery, the complete set of controls, and connection stability are not guaranteed for those models.",
